  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n\n- ${\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$",
  "worked_solution": "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
